{
  "sn24.71:0.1": "Linked Discourses 24.71 ",
  "sn24.71:0.2": "4. The Fourth Round ",
  "sn24.71:0.3": "Winds ",
  "sn24.71:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn24.71:1.2": "“Mendicants, when what exists, because of grasping what and insisting on what, does the view arise: ",
  "sn24.71:1.3": "‘Winds don’t blow; rivers don’t flow; pregnant women don’t give birth; the moon and stars neither rise nor set, but stand firm like a pillar’?” ",
  "sn24.71:1.4": "“Our teachings are rooted in the Buddha. …” ",
  "sn24.71:2.1": "“When form exists, because of grasping form and insisting on form, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.71:2.2": "‘Winds don’t blow; rivers don’t flow; pregnant women don’t give birth; the moon and stars neither rise nor set, but stand firm like a pillar.’ ",
  "sn24.71:2.3": "When feeling … ",
  "sn24.71:2.4": "perception … ",
  "sn24.71:2.5": "choices … ",
  "sn24.71:2.6": "consciousness exists, because of grasping consciousness and insisting on consciousness, the view arises: ",
  "sn24.71:2.7": "‘Winds don’t blow; rivers don’t flow; pregnant women don’t give birth; the moon and stars neither rise nor set, but stand firm like a pillar.’ ",
  "sn24.71:2.8": "What do you think, mendicants? ",
  "sn24.71:2.9": "Is form permanent or impermanent?” ",
  "sn24.71:2.10": "“Impermanent, sir.” ",
  "sn24.71:2.11": "“But if it’s impermanent, is it suffering or happiness?” ",
  "sn24.71:2.12": "“Suffering, sir.” ",
  "sn24.71:2.13": "“But if it’s imper